 r←CollectSitemapData dummy;list;majors;dates;uniqueMajors;latest;newest;releaseDate;pages;Newest
⍝ Returns a two-column matrix with everything that belongs into the sitemap:
⍝ [;1] the path, relative to the server's base URL
⍝ [;2] the date of the last modification in the format YYYY-MM-DD
⍝ "details" and "major_versions" pages are deliberately excluded: those are not meant to be indexed.
⍝ So are all pages that "robots.txt" tells the crawlers to stay away from.
 Newest←{⊃⌽⍵[⍋⍵]}                                       ⍝ Dates are strings here, so ⌈/ is not an option
 releaseDate←3⊃Reg.Version
 uniqueMajors←latest←⍬
 newest←releaseDate
 list←1 Reg.GetAllPackages G.RegistryPath               ⍝ [;1]=package ID, [;2]=publishing date
 :If 0<≢list
     majors←Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch¨list[;1]
     dates←10↑¨list[;2]                                 ⍝ We want YYYY-MM-DD, nothing else
     uniqueMajors←∪majors
     latest←{Newest dates/⍨majors≡¨⊂⍵}¨uniqueMajors     ⍝ Newest release of every major version line
     newest←Newest dates                                ⍝ Newest release on this Registry
 :EndIf
 pages←⊂(1↑'/')releaseDate
 pages,←⊂(Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages')newest
 pages,←⊂(Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/deprecated-pkgs')newest
 pages,←⊂(Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/groups')newest
 :If G.INI.Exist'LICENSE:names'
 :AndIf 0<≢⊃G.INI.Get'LICENSE:names'
     pages,←⊂(Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/get-licenses')releaseDate
 :EndIf
 r←(↑pages)⍪((⊂Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/versions/'),¨uniqueMajors),[1.5]latest
⍝Done
